  "notes": "A key word in manga and publishing culture. Many famous Japanese manga and novels were first published as serializations.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {連載|れんさい}する (to serialize)\n- {連載|れんさい}{開始|かいし} (start of serialization)\n- {連載|れんさい}{終了|しゅうりょう} (end of serialization)\n- {連載|れんさい}{中|ちゅう} (currently serialized)\n- {連載|れんさい}{漫画|まんが} (serialized manga)\n- {連載|れんさい}を{休|やす}む (take a break from serialization — hiatus)\n\nIn manga culture, a {連載|れんさい} ending is a major event. The term {打|う}ち{切|き}り refers to a serialization being cancelled, while {完結|かんけつ} means a planned conclusion.",
